cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these files, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
title: "Arithmetic Origami · Śūnya Conjecture"
authors:
  - given-names: Sambuddha
    family-names: Sarkar
abstract: |-
  Derived from [0; z] = 1/z, in pure Integers (ℤ) and Rationals (ℚ). Every proof verified in
  Lean. Selected by today's measurement; tested by the next.
  Opening: menu_tasting.pdf, Riemanujan's Thanksgiving Tasting Menu.
  Front page: gazette.pdf. Pages 2 and 3: the free parameters of the Standard Model and ΛCDM;
  the Big Bang beside the origami's levels. Statements: Lean 4 files with their checksums. The
  term tables. The Foldcyclopedia: its public entries.
  README.md says what is claimed and what is not, GLOSSARY.md defines every word, CLAIMS.md
  lists each claim with its file and check. A later state is a new version.

  Workflow Delineation
  Author: Sambuddha Sarkar.
  Computation, Śūnya conjecture and axiom, and the methodology. Definitions, theorems and
  kernel checks formulated, reviewed and validated.
  AI assistance:
  Principal investigation within bounded searches.
  Text, code and computation runs drafted and executed under the author's review.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - integer sequences
  - continued fractions
  - Arithmetic Origami
  - Śūnya conjecture
  - Euclidean algorithm
  - Stern–Brocot tree
  - number theory
  - particle physics
  - nuclear physics
  - cosmology
  - formal methods
